      "reason": "The Release 26 REST schema exposes PriorityList as a scalar string, while the Integration API contract exposes String[]. The REST encoding into ordered PriorityListItem entries, including sort-order representation/defaults, is not established by the cited REST schema; a source-backed adapter and round-trip/resource-leveling evidence remain outstanding."
    },
    {
      "p6_field": "ResourceList",
      "status": "pending",
      "reason": "The canonical Shared Core domain and snapshot path preserve ResourceList as an ordered tuple/JSON array, including resource IDs containing commas. The remaining gap is the external wire adapter: Release 26 REST exposes a scalar string while the Integration API exposes String[], and the cited REST schema does not establish a lossless encoding/escaping rule. Keep this field pending until a source-backed REST adapter and round-trip/resource-leveling evidence exist."
    }
